    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\n-- To be done --\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIt would be great if mini.nvim could provide some alternatives for:\r\n- [ ] https://github.com/andymass/vim-matchup\r\n- [ ] https://github.com/tpope/vim-sleuth\r\n- [ ] https://github.com/ziontee113/color-picker.nvim\r\n- [ ] https://github.com/simrat39/symbols-outline.nvim",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestions!\r\n\r\nRight now, the priorities of which module to write next are a mix of \"I am using it right now\" and \"There is an interesting design/implementation idea I want to write\". None of these fall into any of the categories, so it will be a while.\r\n\r\nRight now I'd say that:\r\n- 'symbols-outline.nvim' will probably not happen, as it is based on LSP and I'd like to stay away from it if possible.\r\n- Color picker might be on the horizon, but definitely not close.\r\n- Others might happen.",
